AB  - A novel mass production method of lithium titanite (Li2TiO3) tritium breeder ceramic pebbles using polyvinyl alcohol (PVA) and polyvinyl pyrrolidone (PVP) assisted granulation method (APG) was proposed. A binder solution of polyvinyl alcohol (PVA) was used to modify the Li2TiO3 precursor powder. The powders with adhesive properties were prilled to form green pebbles (GPs) by spheronization at a low rotation speed and spraying with polyvinyl pyrrolidone (PVP), in several cycles. Then, the density and the crush load of the GPs were improved by high-speed rolling. Finally, the ceramic pebbles were produced by sintering. The phase, the microstructure, and the crush load of the ceramic pebbles were characterized by X-ray diffraction (XRD), scanning electron microscopy (SEM), and with a universal tester, respectively.
