FX  - The Sydney Diabetes Prevention Program (SDPP) was a collaboration between the Sydney Local Health District (formerly Sydney South West Area Health Service), The Boden Institute of Obesity, Nutrition, Exercise & Eating Disorders at the University of Sydney, three Divisions of General Practice (Southern Highlands, Macarthur and Central Sydney) and the Australian Diabetes Council (formerly Diabetes Australia-NSW). It was funded by the New South Wales Ministry of Health as part of its commitment to the Australian Better Health Initiative. The SDPP would not have been possible without the perseverance and hard work of the Program Coordinators, Lifestyle Officers, General Practitioners and Practice staff. Most importantly, the participants who so generously provided their information.
